- T243 (completion, queue #108): build sha c79885d2 stands (18,170 B), segment 15.000 s. Cures: (1) hold positions CONFIG-derived + instants printed (P10 completeAtMs+500 → CONFIG-derived, e.g. completeAtMs + holdMs/4; P6 prints evaluated instant); (2) CP13000 fixed leg stands as LITERAL 11400 ms distinct from its derived companion, and every census companion (CP6000·CP7000·CP8000·CP10000·CP12000·CP13000) files evaluated instant + full-predicate result under the timing swap (strikes1DurMs 2000→3000); (3) A13 index ONE entry per census pair naming CONFIG expression, evaluated instant, raw result; ORD labels receipt prints evaluated instant (labelsStart − 1 = 3799 ms). Same completion form.
- T244 (first attempt, queue #109): Packet #14 (@ensan.besham "Hope = Failure (?)") @ throughout — karaoke word-highlight captions as the transcript device. Mechanics (techniques-word-animation.md §T244, read firsthand): the creator's own burned-in captions sit in a fixed bottom band; the currently spoken word renders in full white while the rest of the line sits dimmed, so the highlight sweeps the line in reading order, word by word, locked to the voice. In a faceless piece the moving highlight is the persona's visible speech act. Evidence: ev/066-house-scene.jpg · ev/080-house-clock-verdict.jpg · clips/000-bayes-board-build.mp4 in digest 2026-11-18-ig-dffiipmmac3. Precedent: T195 spoken-state highlight sweep (PASS 88.6, Wave 32) — note the fleet no-captions law boundary (§6.5/§6.6): here the caption IS the technique's subject, as with T195/T196/T197's text; the recreation proves the highlight-sweep effect, production decides lawful adoption. Consumer: DLC assembler word-animation / narration surfaces. Variables: line text, word count, per-word onset/dwell timings, highlight/dim intensities, band geometry, palette, scale. Schedule basis to be named in per-item Plan (A7).

